    "inspectedOn": "2026-10-16",
    "scope": "Six actually inspected exterior photographs plus standard viewer PMTiles/DEM.No bespoke survey sources or redistributed pictures.",
    "pictures": [
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vista_aerea_cupole_catania.jpg",
        "author": "GiovanniPen",
        "date": "2024-04-20",
        "license": "CC-BY-SA-4.0",
        "observed": "Inspected elevated southeast city view: tall ribbed cathedral dome/lantern,lower attached red roofs and heavy eastern stone walls;separate Badia dome and neighboring city roofs remain outside this model. Distant/cropped elevations do not give measured heights."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cathedral_Catania_facade.jpg",
        "author": "Saggittarius A",
        "date": "2017-04-11",
        "license": "CC-BY-SA-4.0",
        "observed": "Inspected close west facade: blue-grey wall fields and pale projecting stone columns/pilasters,layered cornices,central rectangular portal under curved pediment,upper round niche with statuary and triangular top/cross. Side facade/base partly cropped;fine carving and figures are simplified."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cattedrale_di_Sant%27Agata_2024a.jpg",
        "author": "Antony-22",
        "date": "2024-04-23",
        "license": "CC-BY-SA-4.0",
        "observed": "Inspected full west/north oblique: broad three-portal front,round side oculi,high central tiers with paired columns and pediment/cross;long lower grey nave side with pale bay divisions,regular windows and pale balustrade/pinnacle cornice. Main dome and lower clock-cap tower behind. Trees hide some north base and parvis."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Catania_-_Cattedrale_-_2018-07-25.jpg",
        "author": "Eleassar",
        "date": "2018-07-25",
        "license": "CC-BY-SA-4.0",
        "observed": "Inspected elevated north view: tall round drum with paired pale pilasters and narrow lights,grey ribbed dome and small open lantern/cross. Bell tower foreground has a large arched belfry below an upper framed stage;side clock face is partly hidden. Lower tiled roofs and stone apses are visible. No exact height or structural plan inferred."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Badia_di_Sant%27Agata_(Catania)_06_02_2026_67.jpg",
        "author": "Effems",
        "date": "2026-02-06",
        "license": "CC0-1.0",
        "observed": "Inspected north bell-tower/dome close view: open bell arch and balustrade,pale columns,upper square clock stage with visible side dial,small ribbed cap and open little lantern in front of the larger cathedral dome. The clock-stage front is a plain framed panel;both caps are separate forms."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Catania_-_Cattedrale_di_Sant%27Agata_absidi.jpg",
        "author": "Luca Aless",
        "date": "2016-07-29",
        "license": "CC-BY-SA-4.0",
        "observed": "Inspected east-side apses: massive grey-brown lava-stone curved walls with narrow pointed lights and blind arch rhythm,small rectangular attic vents and very shallow tiled caps. Courtyard/lane and lower base partly hidden by vehicles. The dark stone belongs to the apses,not the pale baroque facade."
      }
    ]
